# Register entry merge / unmerge

**Merge deletes exactly one entry** (the duplicate) and leaves the kept entry
untouched — it never sums amounts. Balance entries (`isBalanceEntry`) are never
mergeable.

- Every merge **must write a `RegisterEntryMergeAudit` row in the same
  transaction as the delete**, mirroring all restorable columns of the removed
  entry (`entry*` columns). A merge without an audit row cannot be undone — do
  not delete without auditing.
- `entryDescription` / `entryPlaidId` are `/// @encrypted` on the audit model
  too; do not store decrypted copies elsewhere.
- **Unmerge** (`POST /api/register-entry-unmerge`) re-inserts the removed entry
  with its original id and `entryCreatedAt`, sets `hasBalanceReCalc: true`,
  marks the audit `restoredAt`, and queues a recalculate job. It must reject:
  unknown audits (404), already-restored audits (400), registers the user is
  not a member of (400), and restores whose entry id already exists (400).
- Restored entries lose cascade-deleted relations (e.g. reconciliation items)
  and their stored balance is stale until the recalculate job runs — same
  async-recalc contract as merge.
- `GET /api/register-entry-merge-audits?accountRegisterId=` lists audits
  (unrestored first) for undo UIs (currently the mobile app's "Undo a merge…").
